@startuml
' PROPOSED (not built): verify that a member's phone number is real before they
' can take part in polls. Per-step costs are Twilio list prices checked
' 2026-10-05 (US). See docs/COSTS.md "Phone verification (SMS)" for the monthly
' and election-spike estimates.
title Phone verification (proposed) — who does what, and what each step costs

|Member|
start
:Pays $10/mo via Stripe Checkout\n(existing flow; Stripe keeps ~$0.59);
:Signs in via emailed magic link\n(existing; Resend email, ~free at our volume);
:Enters phone + zipcode\non Complete Profile;

|Backend (Fly.io)|
:Normalise + validate format\n(Twilio Lookup basic: **free**);
:Lookup Line Type + SMS-pumping risk\n(**$0.008**; pumping score free in N. America);
if (Mobile number and low fraud risk?) then (no)
  :Reject: "Please use a mobile number"\n(no text sent, no further cost);
  |Member|
  :Enters a different number;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|Backend (Fly.io)|
:Start verification\n(POST to Twilio Verify);

|Twilio Verify|
:Generate 6-digit code, send SMS\n($0.0083 per text + carrier fee ~$0.004);

|Member|
:Receives text, types the code\ninto the app's verification modal;
if (Code arrived?) then (no — "Resend")
  |Twilio Verify|
  :Send another SMS\n(another ~$0.0125; ~15% of users);
  |Member|
  :Types the new code;
else (yes)
endif

|Backend (Fly.io)|
:Check code with Twilio Verify;

|Twilio Verify|
if (Code correct?) then (yes)
  :Charge **$0.05** per successful verification;
  |Neon Postgres|
  :users.phone_verified_at = now()\n(one row update; negligible compute);
  |Member|
  :Can take part in polls;
  stop
else (no / expired)
  |Member|
  :Shown "wrong or expired code" —\nretry or resend (no $0.05 charge);
  stop
endif

legend right
  **Cost per verified member ≈ $0.066–0.074**
  ($0.05 success + ~1.15 texts × ~$0.0125 + $0.008 Lookup)
  Fly + Neon per verification: ~2 API calls + 1 row update (pennies per 100K)
  The election cost driver is SMS, not Fly/Neon.
endlegend
@enduml
